    "created_at": "2025-11-25T17:34:19Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-11-25T17:34:19Z",
    "body": "Good question. Looks like `type: \"json\"` imports are governed by `connect-src`, so I assume these should be as well. This will require filing a PR against CSP updating the [\"Get the effective directive for _request_\" algorithm](https://w3c.github.io/webappsec-csp/#effective-directive-for-a-request) to list requests with destination `\"text\"` as having effective directive `connect-src`. (Not _strictly_ necessary because `connect-src` is the fallback, but it would be weird to leave it out given that `\"json\"` imports are listed explicitly.)\r\n\r\nFor clarity it might be good to rename the destination to `\"text-import\"` or something, incidentally.\r\n\r\nAnyway, yes, this ends up letting you get the exact same content as `fetch`.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/3576772204/reactions",
